{{define "pagename"}}audit{{end}}
{{define "title"}}Audit trail{{end}}
{{define "body"}}
{{- /* Three different empties, three different sentences. Collapsing them is how a page
       that could not look reports a quiet house. */ -}}
{{if .NoTrail}}
<p class="banner">No trail file exists at the configured path yet, so nothing has been
recorded. It appears the first time the daemon writes an event.</p>
{{else if and .User (not .Rows)}}
<p class="banner">None of the {{.Scanned}} most recent {{if eq .Scanned 1}}event is{{else}}events
are{{end}} for <strong>{{.User}}</strong>.
{{- /* Whether anything older exists is a fact the page can actually know, and the two
       answers point the operator in opposite directions. A full window means the read
       stopped early; a short one with nothing unreadable means the trail ends here and
       there is no older generation to go looking in. */ -}}
{{- if .Truncated}} Older events for that account may exist beyond this window; the filter
only sees the most recent {{.Scanned}}.
{{- else if .Partial}} Nothing older is in what could be read, and the note above says a
generation was left out.
{{- else}} The trail holds nothing older than these, so the search saw every event it can
show.{{end}}
{{- /* A different question from what the trail holds, and the one the operator actually
       asked. Only ever rendered when the account listing answered and nothing matched, so
       it cannot contradict rows on screen and cannot be a guess about a read that failed.
       Phrased about now, because an account deleted last week still owns the events it
       made. */ -}}
{{- if .UserUnknown}} There is no local account named <strong>{{.User}}</strong> on this
machine right now, and account names are case-sensitive, so the spelling may be what failed
here.{{end}}</p>
{{else if not .Rows}}
<p class="banner">The trail is empty. The file exists and holds no readable events.</p>
{{end}}

{{- /* A generation that could not be opened. The rows below are real; they are not all
       there is, and saying only the first half would understate what happened. */ -}}
{{if .Partial}}
<aside class="banner" role="alert">
  The trail is incomplete: a rotated generation could not be read. What is shown is what
  could be read, not everything that happened. The daemon's log names the file.
</aside>
{{end}}

<form method="get" action="/audit" class="filters">
  <label for="user">Account</label>
  <input id="user" name="user" type="text" value="{{.User}}" placeholder="filter by account">
  <button type="submit">Filter</button>
  {{- /* A link, not a second submit button: clearing a GET filter is navigating, and a
       reset button would leave the typed text in the box while showing everything. */ -}}
  {{if .User}}<a href="/audit">Show all</a>{{end}}
</form>

{{if .Rows}}
<table class="rows">
  <caption>{{len .Rows}} of the {{.Scanned}} most recent events, newest first{{if .User}}
    for {{.User}}{{end}}.</caption>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th scope="col">When</th>
      <th scope="col">Event</th>
      <th scope="col">Account</th>
      <th scope="col">Rule</th>
      <th scope="col">Detail</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    {{range .Rows}}
    {{- /* data-label is not decoration: below 40rem the stylesheet turns each row into a
         block and prints the heading from the cell's own data-label, because the column
         header it used to sit under is gone. A column added without one is unlabelled at
         phone width and nothing in the desktop layout notices. */ -}}
    <tr>
      <td data-label="When">
        <time datetime="{{.At.Format "2006-01-02T15:04:05Z07:00"}}">
          {{.At.Format "2006-01-02 15:04:05 MST"}}
        </time>
      </td>
      <td data-label="Event">{{.Kind}}</td>
      <td data-label="Account">{{if .Username}}{{.Username}}{{else}}<span class="muted">nobody</span>{{end}}</td>
      <td data-label="Rule">
        {{- /* The name an operator recognises, with the id underneath: a rename leaves the
             id, and the id is what a bug report has to quote. */ -}}
        {{if .RuleName}}{{.RuleName}}{{end}}
        {{- if .RuleID}}<span class="muted">{{if .RuleName}} ({{.RuleID}}){{else}}{{.RuleID}}{{end}}</span>{{end -}}
      </td>
      <td data-label="Detail">{{.Detail}}</td>
    </tr>
    {{end}}
  </tbody>
</table>
{{end}}

{{- /* What the read cost. Skipped is the difference between "49 events" and "49 of 51
       lines": a trail with unreadable lines is a trail that is losing history, and a
       table that says nothing about it looks clean. */ -}}
<aside class="notes" aria-label="How this list was produced">
  <h2>How this list was produced</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>{{.FilesRead}} {{if eq .FilesRead 1}}trail file was{{else}}trail files were{{end}}
      read, newest first.</li>
    {{if .Skipped}}
    <li>{{.Skipped}} {{if eq .Skipped 1}}line was{{else}}lines were{{end}} present but not
      readable as an event, and skipped.</li>
    {{end}}
    <li>The filter is applied to the events above, not to the whole trail.</li>
  </ul>
</aside>
{{end}}
